From 53e913a1e2d08c51bd15b264940dbc3a8a452ebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:57:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/48] VT100.DSR sends its argument

DSR(n) sent ESC[6n whatever n was, so DSR(5), the device status
report, asked for the cursor position instead. It now sends ESC[<n>n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/VT100.Mod | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/VT100.Mod b/src/runtime/VT100.Mod
index 18c11a72..358068c8 100644
--- a/src/runtime/VT100.Mod
+++ b/src/runtime/VT100.Mod
@@ -297,7 +297,7 @@
 
    PROCEDURE DSR*(n : INTEGER);
    BEGIN
-         EscSeq(6, 'n');
+         EscSeq(n, 'n');
    END DSR;
 
 (* Save Cursor Position *)
